> ss estimate (from 1996), as required by the revision protocol; legal origin, one of their excluded instruments, is not available and is dropped. System GMM: two-step, collapsed instruments, consumpt
> ion, interaction and investment endogenous (lags 2 and deeper), income, enrolment and institutions predetermined (lags 1 and deeper), period dummies and the population dependency ratio as standard i
> nstruments; Windmeijer-corrected standard errors. Fixed effects: country and period fixed effects, standard errors clustered by country. Only the timing of government consumption changes across colu
> mn pairs (period mean, first year of the period, last year of the previous period); each panel uses the same sample for all measures. A positive interaction means that better institutions mitigate t
> he growth cost of government size. Panel C: annual panel 1996–2019 (the window of Mollick and Vianna, 2023), government consumption interacted with the mean of the six WGI indicators (centred), coun
> try and year fixed effects, lagged growth and the controls of Table 1, Driscoll-Kraay standard errors (maximum lag 3); the published text was not available, so the specification follows the descript
> ion in the draft and is an approximate replication only. * p<0.10, ** p<0.05, *** p<0.01.")
